e":0},{"comparison_type":1,"objective_name":"","value":0}],"show_previous_dialog":true,"show_response_options":true,"show_wheel":false,"sound":"","spacing_preset":0,"start_quest":-1,"text":"This is Bucklebury, the chief village of Buckland. Because Buckland is east of the Brandywine, it was not part of the land granted by to the Hobbits by King Argeleb II of Arthedain, and was indeed formed over 300 years after Arthedain ceased to exist. The Hobbits living in Buckland grew a hedge to protect themselves against any evil that may have snuck through the near Old Forest, which bordered Buckland to the east. This 'wall' was named the High Hay or Hay Gate.","text_height":400,"text_offset_x":0,"text_offset_y":0,"text_pitch":1,"text_sound":"minecraft:random.wood_click","text_width":300,"time_availability":0,"title_color":16777215,"title_pos":0,"visual_preset":0}
